# CudaLite OS package set (Debian 13 "trixie", amd64).
# Recommends are disabled (auto/config), so every runtime dependency we want is explicit.
# Each group is justified in docs/report-notes.md.

# --- kernel and live-boot plumbing --------------------------------------------------
# Custom CudaLite kernel (Linux 6.12.107, 281 modules): built by scripts/build_kernel.sh and installed by
# the hook from config/kernel-debs/ (not via config/packages.chroot: live-build 3.0~a57 signs that local
# repository with GnuPG-1-only commands, which fail with Debian 13's GnuPG 2.4).
live-boot
live-config
live-config-systemd
systemd
systemd-sysv
udev
dbus
libpam-systemd
kmod

# --- NVIDIA driver: headless compute only (no Xorg / GL / Vulkan / VDPAU) -----------
# Debian 13 ships the 550 branch = CUDA 12.4 level, matching the host's nvcc 12.4.
nvidia-kernel-dkms
firmware-nvidia-gsp
libcuda1
nvidia-smi
nvidia-modprobe

# --- toolchain DKMS needs to build the module against the exact target kernel -------
dkms
gcc
make

# --- firmware for the laptop's AMD iGPU, which drives the display ------------------
firmware-amd-graphics

# --- base tools ---------------------------------------------------------------------
sudo
ca-certificates
nftables
procps
pciutils
usbutils
iproute2
iputils-ping
less
nano
openssh-client
